WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:05.040
The Enchantress is particularly important
in the story of Beauty And The Beast, however,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.039
in Disney's 1991 animation she only appears
via the stained glass windows during the opening

00:00:10.039 --> 00:00:11.039
prologue.

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:16.500
Disney's 2017 reimagining of the fairy tale
expands her role, casting actress Hattie Morahan,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.679
and giving her character real time on screen
throughout the movie.

00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:23.630
Which means now we can fill in some gaps that
fans have speculated about from the animated

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.630
film.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.140
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I want to delve into the

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.050
character of the Enchantress and explore some
theories about her role in the live-action

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.780
remake of Beauty And The Beast.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.520
Just a quick warning: there are spoilers ahead
for the new Beauty And The Beast movie if

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.690
you haven't seen that yet.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.410
If that's you, tap or click here for my spoiler-free
review and come back and watch this video

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.930
after you've seen the movie.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:49.140
So, the first thing that's significantly different
in Disney's remake is that the introductory

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.800
prologue is actually voiced by the Enchantress
herself.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.660
Her new narration helps to fill in some additional
backstory about the cold-hearted and selfish

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.920
nature of the prince and how he taxed his
people heavily to pay for his lavish parties

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.980
and possessions, which, by the way, feels
like a bit of historical commentary given

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.920
that the new movie is set in the mid-eighteenth
century, a few decades before the French Revolution.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.979
The filmmakers' decision to have the Enchantress
deliver the narration is an interesting one,

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:17.420
because although we don't initially know it,
her character is going to be at the centre

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.810
of many key moments during the new film.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:24.220
And it also points to her role as a sort of
guiding hand over the events of the story.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:28.799
Next, we get to actually see the transformation
of the old woman who appears at the prince's

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:33.579
door into the Enchantress, in a scene very
reminiscent of the flashback scene from The

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:38.469
Enchanted Christmas, an animated Beauty And
The Beast spin-off movie released in 1997.

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:42.371
As well as showing the prince's transformation
into the Beast, the way that the Enchantress

00:01:42.371 --> 00:01:46.820
is bathed in glowing light and appears to
hover in front of the prince is similar in

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.820
both movies.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.840
As for the way she transformed from an old
woman in need of help into a magical being,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.729
that reminded me of the Fairy Godmother's
transformation in Disney's 2015 live-action

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:57.780
remake of Cinderella.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.659
Indeed, the idea of the Enchantress as a sort
of fairy or fairy godmother actually connects

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:07.450
back to the original 18th-century French story
of Beauty And The Beast by Gabrielle-Suzanne

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.450
Barbot de Villeneuve.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:14.340
In fact, in Villeneuve's original story from
1740, there's a good fairy who helps both

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.840
Beauty and the Beast, and this fairy actually
turns out to be Beauty's aunt, as unknown

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.709
to Beauty, her mother was also a fairy.

00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:26.090
Villeneuve's tale also features an old fairy
who looked after the prince while his mother

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:30.700
the queen was defending the kingdom, but later
in the story, this wicked old fairy cursed

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.790
the prince, turning him into a beast, simply
because he refused to marry her.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.010
Disney's animated and live-action films combine
these different good and bad fairies into

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.760
one person: the Enchantress, who encompasses
various aspects of their characters.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:50.050
And interestingly enough, in the Disney novel
"As Old As Time: A Twisted Tale", the Enchantress

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.740
is actually Belle's mother!

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.110
But, I wonder whether in this live-action
version of Beauty And The Beast, it's the

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:59.650
Prince's dead mother who has sent the Enchantress
to help redeem her son and set him back on

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.520
the right path from which he's strayed.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.460
Remember, in the family portrait, the Prince's
mother is the only person whose picture hasn't

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.750
been ripped by the Beast, perhaps because
she was the good influence in the family,

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.670
and as Mrs Potts tells us, it was the Prince's
father who turned his son bad, which is what

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.739
ultimately led to the curse.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:22.760
If that's all true, then in this film, the
Enchantress is basically acting 'in loco parentis',

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.290
in other words, 'in the place of a parent',
and by teaching the prince a lesson is, therefore,

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.090
fulfilling the role his mother can no longer
play.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:34.959
Now, I'm sure many of you made the connection
that the beggar woman Agathe is the same person

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:39.129
as the Enchantress, who seems to have disguised
herself in this way so she can move freely

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:43.260
without the townspeople paying her much attention,
which means she can keep an eye on events

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.269
and even influence them somewhat.

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:49.650
Agathe first appears when Gaston points her
out to Belle as a warning about the consequences

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.989
of what happens to unmarried women after their
fathers die.

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:57.260
And the next time we see Agathe is when she
comes to help Maurice after Gaston and LeFou

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.700
abandon him to the wolves.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.621
This is a moment that shows the compassionate
and kind side of the Enchantress, and after

00:04:02.621 --> 00:04:07.180
she takes Maurice back to her makeshift home
in the woods she gives him hot tea, or perhaps

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.159
some magic concoction, and helps him get better.

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:12.700
By the way, did you notice the owl in these
scenes?

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.700
It's interesting because in medieval Europe,
owls were often associated with wise-women

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.700
and witches.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.110
And in some symbolism, they're connected to
magical forces and the idea of being able

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.490
to see beyond your immediate reality, which
is a nice metaphor for the story of Beauty

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.490
And The Beast.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.700
Now, given the owl's symbolism, the fact that
Agathe has one is a nice way to hint that

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.730
she's connected with the character of the
Enchantress and therefore has a lot more power

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.560
than the townspeople would assume a beggar
woman would have.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.070
With all that in mind, it's also intriguing
that in the original animated movie, an owl

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:46.750
appeared to Maurice and Phillipe just before
Maurice took the wrong turning on his way

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.230
to the fair.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:52.351
And in the new movie, given the way she watches
over events, it's implied that the Enchantress

00:04:52.351 --> 00:04:56.280
caused the lightning strike to fell the tree
that blocked Maurice's path and led him into

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.220
the enchanted part of the forest.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.960
By the way, when I interviewed Beauty And
The Beast director Bill Condon recently, he

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.850
told me that the cane the Enchantress uses
at the start of the film is the same shape

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.630
as the branch that came down in front of Maurice.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.630
You could also argue that the Enchantress
guided subsequent events that led Maurice

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.980
to the Beast's castle, even the wolves chasing
him there.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.720
And by steering Maurice towards the castle,
she seems to have been hoping to give the

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.220
cursed prince an opportunity to interact with
someone from the outside world and redeem

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.220
himself.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.660
Which is what eventually happens when he meets
Belle.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.490
Agathe was also present during the mob scene,
observing the events, and she quietly entered

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:36.120
the castle during the final battle between
the mob and the enchanted objects.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.370
And it's there where she witnesses the true
love Belle and Beast have for each other.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.930
What's really interesting in this scene is
that Belle isn't actually the one who breaks

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:44.930
the curse.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.530
The last petal falls before Belle declares
her love for Beast and so the enchanted characters

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:53.560
are condemned to stay inanimate objects and
Beast himself already appears to have died

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.400
from the wounds inflicted by Gaston.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.900
But when the Enchantress sees how much Belle
loves Beast, she takes control and reverses

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.590
the curse, bringing the rose petals back to
life.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.690
She envelops the Beast in the petals and a
magical energy that revives him and transforms

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.590
him back into his human form.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.800
Then the enchanted characters also come back
to life in their human forms, the crumbling

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.960
castle is restored, and winter melts away
to spring, with the sun rising over the previously

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.090
dark castle and grounds.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:21.880
Given the Enchantress's guiding hand in these
events, I wonder whether she also caused the

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.880
castle rampart to crumble below Gaston's feet,
sending him plummeting to his death!

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.660
After all, at the start of the film, Gaston
did use the example of Agathe and the fact

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:35.310
she's a spinster reduced to begging, as a
way to try to control Belle and curb her independence.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:40.160
And he also tried to kill Maurice, then lied
about it and undermined Agathe as a witness,

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:43.330
calling her 'a filthy hag' in front of the
rest of the town.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.970
The decision by the filmmakers to give more
screen time to the character of the Enchantress

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.710
aka Agathe in the new version is an interesting
one and I'm sure fans will debate her motives

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.880
and to what extent she could be considered
a good character or a cruel one, much as fans

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.950
have done with her character in the animated
movie.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:02.400
However, I do think that the filmmakers have
given the character more agency in the live-action

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.100
version, beefing up her role as a kind of
subversive woman, who lives on the edge of

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.430
society and its expectations.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.090
Just like the updating of Belle's character,
the updating of the Enchantress's character

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:16.630
is, in a way, in tune with Villeneuve's original
French story, which tackled themes and issues

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:21.360
important to 18th-century women, and it's
also in tune with how screenwriter Linda Woolverton

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:25.660
wanted her version of the tale in the animated
movie to be more relevant to contemporary

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:30.000
audiences by making Belle more independent
back in 1991.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.970
And I also think that the filmmakers have
made an effort to humanise the Enchantress,

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.550
changing her from a character you only see
talked about via a stained glass window to

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.830
someone who can show compassion at various
moments in the story.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.460
And you could even argue that her decision
to curse the prince and those around him was

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:48.190
for the good of his kingdom as before this
he had little love in his heart and treated

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.480
his subjects poorly taxing them excessively.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:55.221
As for the idea of punishing his servants
as well, that's fixed to an extent in the

00:07:55.221 --> 00:07:59.990
new version as it's made clear that they were
not blameless as they didn't try to stop the

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:04.090
prince, though I'd imagine if they had stood
up to him they would simply have been dismissed.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:08.440
However, Mrs Potts does tell Belle that the
servants bear some responsibility for how

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:13.030
the prince turned out like his cruel father
who she says 'twisted him up to be just like

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:15.170
him', and they did nothing to prevent it.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:19.220
Now, I'd love to know what you thought about
the Enchantress and the changes to the character

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.110
in the new version of Beauty And The Beast.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:23.520
And how did you like the ending to the new
movie?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.320
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

